{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966795,"nonce":"LNisa/qEHwRJCC4xwqhjZEebS6c=","title":"DSL `lower_reactive_args` must recognize wrapped getter Shape A'","message":"`lower_reactive_args` (the pass that expands `Reactive\u003cT\u003e` prop slots into `(tag, payload)` FFI pairs) MUST recognize Shape A' — the wrapped getter call `__signal_get_by_id_\u003cT\u003e(\u003cid_literal\u003e)` — in addition to bare-Variable signal refs (Shape A), `computed { … } : T` (Shape B), and literals (Shape C).\n\n**Why:** `resolve_dotted_fsm_field_access` rewrites `Ticker.pct` to a bare `Variable(__fsm_ctx_Ticker_pct)`, and then `resolve_signal_calls` force-wraps every ctx-signal Variable into `__signal_get_by_id_\u003cT\u003e(\u003cid_lit\u003e)` so action-body arithmetic and f-string interp compile (a bare reference would be an undefined local). The wrapped form survives into the reactive arg slot. Before the fix `signal_id_for_variable` only matched bare Variables, the call fell through to LITERAL, and the value snapped to its initial constant for the entire session — symptom: `cn.Progress(value = Ticker.pct)` shows the bar at 0 forever even though FSM dispatches are firing and `Ticker.pct` is being mutated.\n\n**How to apply:** When adding a new lowering pass that consumes reactive-prop args, check BOTH the styling-overlay pass and the reactive-args pass for the same Shape A' recognizer. Both passes see the same wrapped-getter shape post-`resolve_signal_calls`, and they need symmetric coverage. The recognizer is roughly:\n\n```rust\nfn signal_id_for_wrapped_getter(value, inner_ty) -\u003e Option\u003cu64\u003e {\n    let Call { callee: Variable(name), positional_args } = value else { return None };\n    let want = match inner_ty { F64 =\u003e \"__signal_get_by_id_f64\", I32 =\u003e \"...\", ... };\n    if name != want { return None; }\n    let Literal::Integer(id_lit) = positional_args.first()? else { return None };\n    Some(id_lit as u64)\n}\n```\n\nRelated: [[gotcha-element-builder-trait-forwarding]] (other half of the same cn-DSL reactivity bringup — wrapper trait method forwarding for click routing / class matching).","files":null}]}